      en: "Cristo Rei (Lubango) is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Angola. The Cristo Rei statue overlooks the city of Lubango from a 2,100-meter-high mountain. Erected in 1957, the white marble statue was modeled after the famous monument in Rio de Janeiro. Erected in 1957. White marble statue. Overlooks Lubango. This landmark is part of the cultural heritage of Angola. Like many notable places in Angola, it combines regional character with wider significance. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Angola."
